<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.7.6.8 DHCPv4_CLIENT_REACQUISITION_07: if the lease expires
  before the client receives a DHCPACK, the client moves to INIT state
  and MUST immediately stop any other network processing (RFC 2131
  §4.4.5).

  Case shape:
    the DUT is brought to BOUND and then left past its lease with no
    server answering. The tester addresses a UDP request to the
    now-expired address; the DUT must not answer it. An expired lease
    means the address is no longer the DUT's to use.

  Pragmatic interpretation under tc8-dut: the spec's pass criterion
  ("DUT does not send UDP") is operationalised on the DHCPv4 BPF
  capture surface as "DUT MUST NOT continue emitting DHCPREQUEST with
  ciaddr equal to the released IP after lease expiration." The
  released IP is the offered IP from the prior ACK; a conformant DUT
  clears ciaddr on INIT-return (see runBoundPhaseMachine's lease_end
  branch + runLoop's outer-cycle reset of committed_lease_be_).

  Trait registers OFFER + ACK on the first two listening states; no
  T1/T2 reply, so the lease expires naturally and the DUT enters
  INIT. The s5_deadline-driven absence window observes any phantom
  REQUEST carrying the released ciaddr (= conformance bug) and
  fails on it; otherwise the deadline passes the case.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="dhcpv4_client_reacquisition_07"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="listening_for_discover">
  <sce:use template="../_templates/dhcpv4_lease_release_no_udp.sce-template.xml"/>
</scxml>
